<%# The rules no distribution can reach. Local: `presenter` (BudgetPagePresenter).

    A band of its own, because the main list is the FILL ORDER and these are not in it: a rule
    that caps a category and a rule on a pool no account holds both ask for money that no
    distribution will ever hand them. Rendering them among the groups would put rows in a
    sequence they are not part of.

    Silent when there are none — an empty "Not in the fill order" heading invents a problem out
    of a healthy screen.

    `data-orphan-group` AND NOT `data-pool-group`: this band is not a pool and must not share the
    pools' selector namespace. It did, keyed on the literal string "Not in the fill order", so a
    pool a user actually named that would collide with it — and the fill-order assertion that
    plucks `data-pool-group` was silently asserting a sequence of pools with a band on the end. %>
<% orphans = presenter.orphan_rules %>
<% if orphans.any? %>
  <section class="bg-white border border-status-danger rounded" data-orphan-group>
    <div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 bg-status-danger-light flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-status-danger">Not in the fill order</h3>
      <span class="text-sm text-status-danger">no distribution reaches these</span>
    </div>

    <% orphans.each do |rule| %>
      <%= render "rule_row", rule: rule %>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
